WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.335
-What's happening, everybody?
How you doing?

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.136
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.136 --> 00:00:06.272
Yeah.
This can't be zipped.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:09.542
So FYI.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:12.779
I don't care if you
offer me $5 million,

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:16.149
I'd have to politely decline.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:20.319
News is crazy.
Protests every week, riots.

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.021
We used to have riots
every 30 years.

00:00:22.021 --> 00:00:23.722
Now they have riots every week.

00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:25.725
I feel bad
for everybody in a riot,

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:29.529
but I really feel bad
for the fat riot cop.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.097
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:33.266
'Cause you know
he was just home, chillin'.

00:00:33.266 --> 00:00:35.267
The phone rang,
"There's a riot!

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:36.870
Get your riot gear on!

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.938
Be downtown in 20 minutes!"

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:42.909
And he's like, "I haven't worn
that stuff in nine years."

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:46.178
[ Laughter ]
"Honey, I'm getting fired.

00:00:46.178 --> 00:00:48.214
I wore it for Halloween
three years a--

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:51.017
Do we still have it?
It's not gonna fit."

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:54.720
And she's like, "You never know.
Just try it on!

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.722
You never --
You're doing so good.

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:58.658
I can see it right here."

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:00.326
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.461
He's like,
"Are you looking at me?

00:01:02.461 --> 00:01:04.197
Look at me from the side."

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:05.331
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:08.167
"We know it's not gonna fit."

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.870
"Be positive!"

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.739
"Honey,
I just hate a whole pizza.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:15.074
Hot dogs were in the crust."

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:16.442
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:19.913
"I was dipping that in
the queso dip behind your back.

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:22.014
We know."

00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:24.016
But she still gets him
to show up with the riot,

00:01:24.016 --> 00:01:26.618
the helmet
just on top of his head.

00:01:26.618 --> 00:01:30.890
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.558
The visor's -- Yeah.

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:34.660
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:37.430
The visor's all fogged up.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.833
The vest isn't covering any
vital organs, just his boobs.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:42.769
If he gets the boob shot,
he lives.

00:01:42.769 --> 00:01:44.470
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.606
Yeah, you never even saw
the fat riot cop before.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:47.874
You'll never not see him now.

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:49.609
Every riot, you're gonna be
like, "Where is he?

00:01:49.609 --> 00:01:51.177
There he is right there, look.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:54.046
He looks like the float
in a Macy's day parade.

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:57.950
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.251
I think
it's 'cause I'm getting older.

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:01.587
I'm getting older, and, uh...
I don't like my friends.

00:02:01.587 --> 00:02:04.089
I think the older you get --
It's true.

00:02:04.089 --> 00:02:05.824
The older you get,
the smaller your group gets.

00:02:05.824 --> 00:02:08.828
Have you noticed that?
In your 20s, groups are huge.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.464
"Let's all go together!

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.733
All 78 of us.
Friends for life!"

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.001
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.535
The older you get,
you're like, "Are they going?

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:18.571
'Cause if they're going,
I'm not going, 'cause...

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:21.174
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, I hate his wife's face."

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:26.746
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.881
I think 'cause when you're in
your 20s, time doesn't matter.

00:02:28.881 --> 00:02:30.183
Time, you know, it's like,

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.051
you know,
"We're gonna live forever!

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.085
Friends for life!

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:35.054
My hair is always
gonna be here!"

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.290
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:40.993
I have 30 summers left.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:44.163
Yeah.
That's a real number.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:47.967
I don't have time
for crappy people in my life.

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.102
I've dumped my friends.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:50.970
I have one friend,
I can't stand him.

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.605
He's Italian,
not even full-blooded,

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:54.240
till we go
to an Italian restaurant,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.442
and all of a sudden,
he's off the boat from Sicily.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:57.743
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.743 --> 00:02:59.178
It's like,
"What you are gonna get?"

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.314
"I don't know. I'm thinking of
getting the pasta fagioli."

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.783
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:06.386
Who are you?
What's your name?

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:08.154
The waiter doesn't --
He's from Mexico.

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:11.591
He doesn't understand
a word you're saying,<i> Sean!</i>

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:15.228
[ Laughter ]
I --

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:18.665
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.499
I have another friend --
Oh, I can't stand him.

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:22.201
He loves telling stories.
You have that friend?

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:24.069
"Dude, I got a story."
"Great."

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:26.138
And his stories stink.
They just stink.

00:03:26.138 --> 00:03:27.807
And they're boring,
but he thinks they're awesome,

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:30.009
'cause in the story,
he always says, "True story,"

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.611
like you're not believing it.

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:34.280
And you are, 'cause
they're just boring stories.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.682
I'm like,
"Stop saying 'true story.'

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:37.750
You're not a Navy S.E.A.L."

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.619
Navy S.E.A.L.s
can say, "True story."

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.153
Their stories are epic.

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:43.756
Their stories are like, "Dude, I
killed five guys with a nickel."

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.725
"Wh-a-at?"
"True story!"

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:48.694
Yeah! Thp! Thp!
[ Imitating choking ]

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:50.363
"This is the nickel."

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:54.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.601
His stories stinks.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:56.903
He's like,
"Dude, I just went to Aruba.

00:03:56.903 --> 00:03:57.970
I got a story for you."

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.305
I'm like,
"Oh, this should suck."

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.140
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.776
He goes, "Me and my wife,
on the beach, water's edge,

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:06.345
sun setting.
We look out at the ocean.

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:09.882
At the last second, dolphin
came up out of the water."

00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:11.283
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:11.283 --> 00:04:13.586
"True story."

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:16.022
"Yeah, yeah, I, uh --
I believe it.

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.690
It's the ocean.
That's their home."

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.891
[ Laughter ]

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.993
"That's where dolphins
do that kind of stuff.

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.694
Did it happen
in the parking lot?

00:04:22.694 --> 00:04:25.631
Did it come out of asphalt
from under a Honda Civic

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:27.366
and murder
an old lady on a lark?

00:04:27.366 --> 00:04:28.901
That's nuts.
I wouldn't believe that."

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.336
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:33.272
If you say, "True story,"
the story should epic.

00:04:33.272 --> 00:04:35.875
The person's eyebrows
should be like, "Wh-a-a-at?!"

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:37.343
True stories should be nuts.

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:40.212
Like, "Dude, check this out.
A month ago, I was on my couch,

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:43.382
I looked over,
my dog's bunghole opened up."

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:44.751
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:48.320
"I heard angels go..."
[ Vocalizing ]

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:49.922
"A pearl fell out."

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.525
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.961
"My wife walked in, went,
"I was looking for that,"

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:58.263
picked it up, put it on her ear,
left, haven't seen her since.

00:04:58.263 --> 00:05:00.399
True story.
True story."

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:01.500
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:03.269
Thank you very much, everybody.

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:05.037
Thank you so much.
Thank you!

00:05:05.037 --> 00:05:08.308
♪♪

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:11.443
How you doing, my friend?
-Thanks a lot.

00:05:11.443 --> 00:05:13.045
-Robert Kelly!

00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:15.214
[ Cheers and applause ]
That is how you do it!

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:19.052
For more info on Robert,
go to robertkellylive.com.

